 ('sunbite',"Don't Bite the Sun",'Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don%27t_Bite_the_Sun','secondary_reference','Four-BEE residents’ needs, government, repair and bodily renewal are handled by quasi-robots; the narrator struggles to find useful work.','A story summary, not a demographic census; desert exile and useful personal creations complicate an absolute leisure claim.'),
 ('marrow','Marrow review','Publishers Weekly','https://www.publishersweekly.com/9780312868017','secondary_review','Human captains operate a vast adjustable-environment passenger ship.','Luxury cruising and immortality do not identify automated household production or the ordinary access contract.'),
 ('redstar','Red Star: The First Bolshevik Utopia','Alexander Bogdanov; edited by Loren R. Graham and Richard Stites, reproduced by Everand','https://www.everand.com/book/392106957/Red-Star-The-First-Bolshevik-Utopia','publisher_excerpt','Accessible book description/editorial material identifies automated factories, inventory coordination, unlimited consumption and voluntary unpaid work.','The bounded indexed/presented description was used, not the entire subscription ebook; central statistics are not autonomous AI government.'),
 ('redstar-summary','Red Star','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Star_(novel)','secondary_reference','Common housing standards, voluntary job changes and widespread chosen work on Mars.','Martians are an explicit organic-person comparison, not silently classified as humans; almost all working is not an all-age census.'),
 ('andromeda','Andromeda: A Space-Age Tale','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andromeda_(novel)','secondary_reference','Great Circle communist Earth, active scientists and explorers, and technological context.','This short summary does not establish ordinary automated production and the access mechanism.'),
 ('bull',"The Bull’s Hour",'Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bull%27s_Hour','secondary_reference','Tormance’s oligarchy and deliberately unequal lifespans and occupations.','Social oppression does not itself establish deliberate suppression of labor-replacing technology.'),
 ('circle','The Final Circle of Paradise','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Final_Circle_of_Paradise','secondary_reference','The resort city’s affluent consumption, pleasure technologies and cultural critique.','The summary does not clearly identify productive automation or a labor-independent necessities entitlement.'),
 ('sun-city','Незнайка в Солнечном городе','Wikipedia contributors','https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/Незнайка_в_Солнечном_городе','secondary_reference','Identifies Nosov’s technological city and separates its industrial setting from the visitor’s magic.','Does not by itself specify fabrication and free access.'),
 ('sun-factories','Незнайка на Луне — opening chapter, indexed scan','Nikolay Nosov; scan host Scribd','https://ru.scribd.com/document/1031954541/neznaika','indexed_primary_passage','Opening passage describes clothing machines doing sewing, goods taken according to need as in Sun City, and remaining design work.','Only the short indexed opening passage was used; scan/OCR errors and access limitations remain. No full book or magical manufacturing assumption.'),
 ('moon','Незнайка на Луне','Wikipedia contributors','https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/Незнайка_на_Луне','secondary_reference','Lunar monopolists resist giant food plants; poor residents need wages, food and housing.','Suppressing larger crops or defending property is not by itself a demonstrated automation/employment-preservation regime.'),
 ('geometers','Звёзды — холодные игрушки','Wikipedia contributors','https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/Звёзды_—_холодные_игрушки','secondary_reference','Geometers’ human identity, advanced technology, coercive education and social conformity.','No clear ordinary productive/access mechanism in this bounded reference.'),
 ('arank','Спектр — reader reviews, page 13','Named/handle-based LitRes readers, individual authors not checked','https://www.litres.ru/book/sergei-lukjanenko/spektr-119490/reviews/?page=13','reader_review','A reader describes Arank as a materially affluent needs-oriented technocratic world.','Reader commentary and futuristic cities do not establish how automatic production supports that access; not enough for admission.'),
